A||N||7||Bob Englert||Front End Alignment ???||||1||
Z||000000||Bob Englert||12-23-2000||07:21 PM||||I recently rebuilt the front suspension on my blue 87 GT and took it to the alignment shop.  When I got the car back it has been driving very poorly.  The car has very poor directional stability.  It will be OK for a moment and then want to pull sharply to the right.  Sometimes it pulls left but mostly right.  It is VERY sensitive to any imperfections in the road surface.<P>It feels as though the car suddenly grabs the tire and goes.  Everything is very tight as far as I can tell.  It feels as though the toe is wrong or their is not enough caster for good tracking.  When I first discussed this with the shop they swapped the 2 front tires but this did not affect the problem at all.<P>I will be taking it back to the alignment shop next week.  Can anyone give me some guidance on how the alignment settings might contribute to the problems I am having? Right now the car is no fun to drive at all!<P>Thanks and happy holidays.<P>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>85 SE 4 cyl||||reg||1
Z||000001||PJ||12-23-2000||08:02 PM||||Sounds like the caster is off. Not enough and not equal side to side. You need about 5 degrees positive, +/- .5 side to side. First generation front ends are hard to get right. Some shops refuse to spend the time.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Oreif||12-23-2000||08:32 PM||||Make sure they have the recent spec's. Some of the older alignment machine's have the wrong numbers to set the alignment.||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||12-23-2000||08:44 PM||||do a search on alignment. I posted the full GM specs recently. If you got the printout then you can compair them to that post.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Bob Englert||12-23-2000||09:19 PM||||Thanks for the info.  I will take the car back and have them check it against the numbers and give me a printout.<P>When I did a quick tire tread measurement, it appears that the front end might be toed out.  I will check it again, but this might be the root of my problem.  From the values I found it appears that there should be 0 to a little tow-in. <P>Could a tow-out setting cause some of the problems I am seeing?<P>Thanks again....<P>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>85 SE 4 cyl||||reg||1
Z||000005||MrPBody||12-24-2000||10:21 PM||||For sure, toe-out will cause steering wander.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Dan86gt3.8||12-25-2000||01:32 AM||||man check thoose rear wheels  if they are off that can reek havock (sp?).  My right rear wheel bearing was bad and it made the car turn real funny, suddenly jerk side to side, and made driving the car at 70+ a REAL challenge!<P>------------------<BR>86 gt fiero<BR>3.8/4speed auto<BR>ace conversion kit<BR>1/4- 15.3@90mph||||reg||1
Z||000007||bHooper||12-25-2000||10:12 AM||||bummer, Bob!<P>i hope you get that fixed this week!<P>i am going to spend a bit of time trying to find my rear wiggle, if not i might take it back to the shop, too.<P>hoop||||reg||1
